{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-23435","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24409","text":"PULSE v0.2 — Behavioral Loop Types"}]},{"id":"blk-23436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24410","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-24411","text":" Design proposal (2026-05-27) — for review before implementation."}]},{"id":"blk-23437","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24412","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal:"},{"id":"spn-24413","text":" Promote PULSE from a "},{"id":"spn-24414","marks":["italic"],"text":"structural schema"},{"id":"spn-24415","text":" (named phases + named tokens) to a "},{"id":"spn-24416","marks":["italic"],"text":"typed protocol"},{"id":"spn-24417","text":" (session-typed phases + linear tokens + projected choreography). Bring formal-spec quality to the level of behavioral type systems without losing the implementation maturity of v0.1.1."}]},{"id":"blk-23438","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24418","text":"Why"}]},{"id":"blk-23439","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24419","text":"PULSE v0.1.1 declares 5 phase kinds, 6 cross-loop tokens, and 7 invariants. The schema validates "},{"id":"spn-24420","marks":["italic"],"text":"names and shapes"},{"id":"spn-24421","text":" but cannot answer:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23441","spans":[{"id":"spn-24422","text":"Question v0.1.1 cannot answer"}]},{"id":"blk-23442","spans":[{"id":"spn-24423","text":"What's needed"}]}],"id":"blk-23440","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23443","spans":[{"id":"spn-24424","text":"Is this manifest deadlock-free?"}]},{"id":"blk-23444","spans":[{"id":"spn-24425","text":"Session-typed phase graph"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23445","spans":[{"id":"spn-24426","text":"Will every emitted "},{"id":"spn-24427","marks":["code"],"text":"SurpriseSignal"},{"id":"spn-24428","text":" be consumed?"}]},{"id":"blk-23446","spans":[{"id":"spn-24429","text":"Linear token typing"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23447","spans":[{"id":"spn-24430","text":"Is "},{"id":"spn-24431","marks":["code"],"text":"loop@v2"},{"id":"spn-24432","text":" a safe drop-in replacement for "},{"id":"spn-24433","marks":["code"],"text":"loop@v1"},{"id":"spn-24434","text":"?"}]},{"id":"blk-23448","spans":[{"id":"spn-24435","text":"Behavioral subtyping"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23449","spans":[{"id":"spn-24436","text":"If loop A sends X, will loop B receive a compatible X?"}]},{"id":"blk-23450","spans":[{"id":"spn-24437","text":"Multiparty choreography + projection"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23451","spans":[{"id":"spn-24438","text":"Does this phase's declared effect match its runtime behavior?"}]},{"id":"blk-23452","spans":[{"id":"spn-24439","text":"Effect rows + runtime fidelity check"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23453","spans":[{"id":"spn-24440","text":"Are the declared invariants actually true of this manifest?"}]},{"id":"blk-23454","spans":[{"id":"spn-24441","text":"Refinement-type checker"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24442","text":"Behavioral type systems (session types, multiparty session types, behavioral contracts) answer exactly these questions — but as preprints, not as running software. PULSE v0.2 ports the answers into a JSON-Schema-grounded substrate that already has 5 reference manifests and a conformance suite."}]},{"id":"blk-23456","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24443","text":"What it buys (scorecard delta)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23458","spans":[{"id":"spn-24444","text":"Axis"}]},{"id":"blk-23459","spans":[{"id":"spn-24445","text":"v0.1.1"}]},{"id":"blk-23460","spans":[{"id":"spn-24446","text":"v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-23461","spans":[{"id":"spn-24447","text":"Why"}]}],"id":"blk-23457","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23462","spans":[{"id":"spn-24448","text":"Formality"}]},{"id":"blk-23463","spans":[{"id":"spn-24449","text":"8"}]},{"id":"blk-23464","spans":[{"id":"spn-24450","marks":["bold"],"text":"10"}]},{"id":"blk-23465","spans":[{"id":"spn-24451","text":"Session-type-grade; refinement types on cadence/invariants; effect rows on phases"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23466","spans":[{"id":"spn-24452","text":"Compositionality"}]},{"id":"blk-23467","spans":[{"id":"spn-24453","text":"7"}]},{"id":"blk-23468","spans":[{"id":"spn-24454","marks":["bold"],"text":"10"}]},{"id":"blk-23469","spans":[{"id":"spn-24455","text":"Choreography + projection; linear tokens; behavioral subtyping"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23470","spans":[{"id":"spn-24456","text":"Substrate independence"}]},{"id":"blk-23471","spans":[{"id":"spn-24457","text":"9"}]},{"id":"blk-23472","spans":[{"id":"spn-24458","marks":["bold"],"text":"10"}]},{"id":"blk-23473","spans":[{"id":"spn-24459","text":"Typed protocol portable to any language with a type system"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23474","spans":[{"id":"spn-24460","text":"Closure"}]},{"id":"blk-23475","spans":[{"id":"spn-24461","text":"7"}]},{"id":"blk-23476","spans":[{"id":"spn-24462","marks":["bold"],"text":"9"}]},{"id":"blk-23477","spans":[{"id":"spn-24463","text":"Liveness + fidelity machine-checked; loses 1 for new verifier dependency"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23478","spans":[{"id":"spn-24464","marks":["bold"],"text":"Total / 40"}]},{"id":"blk-23479","spans":[{"id":"spn-24465","marks":["bold"],"text":"31"}]},{"id":"blk-23480","spans":[{"id":"spn-24466","marks":["bold"],"text":"39"}]},{"id":"blk-23481","spans":[{"id":"spn-24467","text":""}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23482","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24468","text":"For external context see "},{"id":"spn-24469","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/V0.2-BEHAVIORAL-TYPES-RATIONALE.md"},{"id":"spn-24470","text":" (planned) which compares this against Agent Behavioral Contracts (preprint), AgentRFC, and the CCS/CSP ceiling."}]},{"id":"blk-23483","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24471","text":"The six additions"}]},{"id":"blk-23484","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24472","text":"1. Typed token registry"}]},{"id":"blk-23485","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24473","marks":["bold"],"text":"File:"},{"id":"spn-24474","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24475","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/pulse-tokens.v0.2.json"},{"id":"spn-24476","text":" (new)"}]},{"id":"blk-23486","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24477","text":"Each canonical token gets a payload schema, a linearity annotation, a variance annotation, and a TTL."}]},{"id":"blk-23487","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"tokens\": {\n    \"TopologyContext\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/topology_context.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 60000,\n      \"description\": \"Emitted by retrieve, consumed by route. Loss would blind routing — must be consumed.\"\n    },\n    \"DeliberationRequest\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/deliberation_request.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 300000,\n      \"description\": \"Triggers an inner deliberation loop. Loss would silently skip κ-resolution.\"\n    },\n    \"DeliberationResult\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/deliberation_result.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 300000\n    },\n    \"OutcomeSignal\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/outcome_signal.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 3600000,\n      \"description\": \"Audit primitive. Every action result must produce one — drop = audit failure.\"\n    },\n    \"ReputationUpdate\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/reputation_update.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"affine\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 86400000,\n      \"description\": \"Long-window aggregation; tolerates loss (drop down from linear because the next update overrides anyway).\"\n    },\n    \"ConsolidationEvent\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/consolidation_event.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"affine\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 3600000,\n      \"description\": \"Housekeeping signal; consolidate is idempotent.\"\n    },\n    \"SurpriseSignal\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/surprise_signal.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 60000,\n      \"description\": \"GRASP forward-model-prediction-error. Must be consumed.\"\n    },\n    \"SessionFidelityViolation\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/session_fidelity_violation.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 86400000,\n      \"description\": \"Runtime-observed protocol violation. Must be reported, never silently dropped.\"\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-23488","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24478","marks":["bold"],"text":"Default for new canonical tokens: `linear`."},{"id":"spn-24479","text":" Authors must explicitly opt down to "},{"id":"spn-24480","marks":["code"],"text":"affine"},{"id":"spn-24481","text":" only when the token is observational, idempotent, or inherently lossy-tolerant (next emission overrides previous). This default flows from OS-010's \"every consequential signal must be audited\" thesis — silent loss is an audit failure; duplication is detected via idempotency keys at the substrate boundary."}]},{"id":"blk-23489","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24482","marks":["bold"],"text":"Linearity values:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23491","spans":[{"id":"spn-24483","text":"Value"}]},{"id":"blk-23492","spans":[{"id":"spn-24484","text":"Meaning"}]},{"id":"blk-23493","spans":[{"id":"spn-24485","text":"Checker enforces"}]}],"id":"blk-23490","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23494","spans":[{"id":"spn-24486","marks":["code"],"text":"linear"}]},{"id":"blk-23495","spans":[{"id":"spn-24487","text":"Exactly-once consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-23496","spans":[{"id":"spn-24488","text":"Emit ⇒ exactly one consumer; consumer is unique"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23497","spans":[{"id":"spn-24489","marks":["code"],"text":"affine"}]},{"id":"blk-23498","spans":[{"id":"spn-24490","text":"At-most-once consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-23499","spans":[{"id":"spn-24491","text":"Emit ⇒ at most one consumer (may drop)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23500","spans":[{"id":"spn-24492","marks":["code"],"text":"relevant"}]},{"id":"blk-23501","spans":[{"id":"spn-24493","text":"At-least-once consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-23502","spans":[{"id":"spn-24494","text":"Emit ⇒ at least one consumer (may duplicate)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23503","spans":[{"id":"spn-24495","marks":["code"],"text":"unrestricted"}]},{"id":"blk-23504","spans":[{"id":"spn-24496","text":"Any consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-23505","spans":[{"id":"spn-24497","text":"No constraint"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23506","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24498","marks":["bold"],"text":"Variance values:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23508","spans":[{"id":"spn-24499","text":"Value"}]},{"id":"blk-23509","spans":[{"id":"spn-24500","text":"Meaning"}]}],"id":"blk-23507","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23510","spans":[{"id":"spn-24501","marks":["code"],"text":"covariant"}]},{"id":"blk-23511","spans":[{"id":"spn-24502","text":"Subtype payloads acceptable on the consumer side"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23512","spans":[{"id":"spn-24503","marks":["code"],"text":"contravariant"}]},{"id":"blk-23513","spans":[{"id":"spn-24504","text":"Supertype payloads acceptable on the producer side"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23514","spans":[{"id":"spn-24505","marks":["code"],"text":"invariant"}]},{"id":"blk-23515","spans":[{"id":"spn-24506","text":"Exact payload schema match required"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23516","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24507","marks":["bold"],"text":"Required payload schemas:"},{"id":"spn-24508","text":" Each token gets its own JSON Schema under "},{"id":"spn-24509","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/tokens/"},{"id":"spn-24510","text":". "},{"id":"spn-24511","marks":["bold"],"text":"Eight"},{"id":"spn-24512","text":" new schema files (the six v0.1.1 canonical tokens + two added in v0.2: "},{"id":"spn-24513","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationRequest"},{"id":"spn-24514","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24515","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionFidelityViolation"},{"id":"spn-24516","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-23517","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24517","text":"Token evolution rules (registry-level subtyping only)"}]},{"id":"blk-23518","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24518","text":"Token payload evolution happens "},{"id":"spn-24519","marks":["bold"],"text":"in the global registry, never per-loop"},{"id":"spn-24520","text":". This flows from OS-010 §1019–1051 (\"canonical tokens stable through v1.0; additive-only without minor bump; vendor-namespacing for custom tokens\")."}]},{"id":"blk-23519","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23521","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24521","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive-only within a minor version."},{"id":"spn-24522","text":" Adding optional fields to a"}]}],"id":"blk-23520","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23522","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24523","text":"token's payload schema is allowed without bumping the token's version. Removing or renaming fields requires a minor version bump and 12-month notice (per OS-010 stability policy)."}]},{"id":"blk-23523","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23525","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24524","marks":["bold"],"text":"Registry tracks the partial order."},{"id":"spn-24525","text":" The registry asserts"}]}],"id":"blk-23524","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-23526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24526","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_context.v0.2 <: topology_context.v0.1"},{"id":"spn-24527","text":" when the v0.2 schema is an additive extension of v0.1. The behavioral subtyping checker (§5) consults the registry rather than re-deriving compatibility."}]},{"id":"blk-23527","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23529","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24528","marks":["bold"],"text":"No per-loop token variants."},{"id":"spn-24529","text":" A loop that needs a custom payload"}]}],"id":"blk-23528","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-23530","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24530","text":"must register a vendor-namespaced token (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24531","marks":["code"],"text":"acme.v1.AcmeOutcome"},{"id":"spn-24532","text":") in the registry and reference it canonically from its manifest. Loops never declare local subtypes of canonical tokens — that would explode the cross-loop vocabulary and break PRISM's ability to benchmark heterogeneous systems against a shared evaluation grammar."}]},{"id":"blk-23531","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24533","text":"2. Phase signatures with effect rows"}]},{"id":"blk-23532","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24534","marks":["bold"],"text":"Change:"},{"id":"spn-24535","text":" Extend the existing "},{"id":"spn-24536","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[]"},{"id":"spn-24537","text":" entries in "},{"id":"spn-24538","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.2.json"},{"id":"spn-24539","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-24540","marks":["code"],"text":"inputs"},{"id":"spn-24541","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24542","marks":["code"],"text":"outputs"},{"id":"spn-24543","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24544","marks":["code"],"text":"effects"},{"id":"spn-24545","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24546","marks":["code"],"text":"successors"},{"id":"spn-24547","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-24548","marks":["code"],"text":"refinements"},{"id":"spn-24549","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-23533","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"retrieve_context\",\n      \"kind\": \"retrieve\",\n      \"inputs\":  { \"tokens\": [], \"substrates\": [\"memory\"] },\n      \"outputs\": { \"tokens\": [\"TopologyContext\"] },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"calls\":    [\"memory.retrieve_context\", \"memory.topology_analyze\"],\n        \"mutates\":  [],\n        \"may_emit\": [],\n        \"external\": []\n      },\n      \"successors\": [\"route_topology\"],\n      \"refinements\": {\n        \"latency_ms_max\": 200,\n        \"deterministic\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"route_topology\",\n      \"kind\": \"route\",\n      \"inputs\":  { \"tokens\": [\"TopologyContext\"], \"substrates\": [] },\n      \"outputs\": { \"tokens\": [] },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"calls\":    [],\n        \"mutates\":  [],\n        \"may_emit\": [\"DeliberationRequest\"],\n        \"external\": []\n      },\n      \"successors\": [\"deliberate\", \"act_node_write\"],\n      \"refinements\": {\n        \"branch_predicate\": \"topology.routing\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-23534","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24550","marks":["bold"],"text":"Effect row fields:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23536","spans":[{"id":"spn-24551","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-23537","spans":[{"id":"spn-24552","text":"What it tracks"}]}],"id":"blk-23535","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23538","spans":[{"id":"spn-24553","marks":["code"],"text":"calls"}]},{"id":"blk-23539","spans":[{"id":"spn-24554","text":"Substrate operation IDs invoked (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24555","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-24556","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24557","marks":["code"],"text":"policy.check_policy"},{"id":"spn-24558","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23540","spans":[{"id":"spn-24559","marks":["code"],"text":"mutates"}]},{"id":"blk-23541","spans":[{"id":"spn-24560","text":"Substrate operation IDs that change state (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24561","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.store_node"},{"id":"spn-24562","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24563","marks":["code"],"text":"audit.append_event"},{"id":"spn-24564","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23542","spans":[{"id":"spn-24565","marks":["code"],"text":"may_emit"}]},{"id":"blk-23543","spans":[{"id":"spn-24566","text":"Token names this phase may produce"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23544","spans":[{"id":"spn-24567","marks":["code"],"text":"external"}]},{"id":"blk-23545","spans":[{"id":"spn-24568","text":"External resources touched (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24569","marks":["code"],"text":"http://*"},{"id":"spn-24570","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24571","marks":["code"],"text":"mcp://prism"},{"id":"spn-24572","text":")"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23546","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24573","marks":["bold"],"text":"Granularity is operation-level, not storage-level."},{"id":"spn-24574","text":" Effect rows reference the substrate API surface defined in OS-010 §9 (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24575","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-24576","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24577","marks":["code"],"text":"audit.append_event"},{"id":"spn-24578","text":"), never specific storage paths like "},{"id":"spn-24579","marks":["code"],"text":"sqlite.kg.nodes"},{"id":"spn-24580","text":". This flows from the \"substrate independence\" thesis: the spec must not assume a relational backend, and graphonomous swapping SQLite for Postgres should not require manifest changes."}]},{"id":"blk-23547","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24581","marks":["bold"],"text":"Refinement values:"},{"id":"spn-24582","text":" key-value predicates. A small vendored evaluator handles the supported subset; unknown keys are passed through as documentation."}]},{"id":"blk-23548","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24583","marks":["bold"],"text":"Supported refinement predicates (vendored mini-evaluator):"}]},{"id":"blk-23549","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23551","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24584","text":"Comparison: "},{"id":"spn-24585","marks":["code"],"text":"≤"},{"id":"spn-24586","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24587","marks":["code"],"text":"<"},{"id":"spn-24588","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24589","marks":["code"],"text":"≥"},{"id":"spn-24590","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24591","marks":["code"],"text":">"},{"id":"spn-24592","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24593","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-24594","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24595","marks":["code"],"text":"!="},{"id":"spn-24596","text":" on numeric or string literals"}]}],"id":"blk-23550","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24597","text":"Boolean conjunction ("},{"id":"spn-24598","marks":["code"],"text":"∧"},{"id":"spn-24599","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-24600","marks":["code"],"text":"&&"},{"id":"spn-24601","text":") and disjunction ("},{"id":"spn-24602","marks":["code"],"text":"∨"},{"id":"spn-24603","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-24604","marks":["code"],"text":"||"},{"id":"spn-24605","text":") over the above"}]}],"id":"blk-23552","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23555","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24606","text":"Set membership: "},{"id":"spn-24607","marks":["code"],"text":"value in [a, b, c]"}]}],"id":"blk-23554","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23557","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24608","text":"Negation of any of the above"}]}],"id":"blk-23556","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23558","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24609","text":"No Z3, no external SMT solver, no optional peer dependency. The vendored evaluator is a few hundred lines of TypeScript in "},{"id":"spn-24610","marks":["code"],"text":"src/refinement.ts"},{"id":"spn-24611","text":" and runs in any environment that runs npm. The ≤25KB processor target from STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW.md applies here too."}]},{"id":"blk-23559","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24612","text":"Recognized refinement keys in v0.2:"}]},{"id":"blk-23560","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23562","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24613","marks":["code"],"text":"latency_ms_max"},{"id":"spn-24614","text":" (number) — checker emits a benchmark assertion"}]}],"id":"blk-23561","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23564","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24615","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic"},{"id":"spn-24616","text":" (boolean) — flagged in conformance T-DET"}]}],"id":"blk-23563","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23566","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24617","marks":["code"],"text":"branch_predicate"},{"id":"spn-24618","text":" (string) — referenced expression must appear in a"}]}],"id":"blk-23565","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23567","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24619","text":"consumed token's payload schema"}]},{"id":"blk-23568","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23570","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24620","marks":["code"],"text":"idempotent"},{"id":"spn-24621","text":" (boolean) — extends existing T03 phase-idempotency check"}]}],"id":"blk-23569","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23572","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24622","marks":["code"],"text":"requires_kappa"},{"id":"spn-24623","text":" (string, e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24624","marks":["code"],"text":"\"== 0\""},{"id":"spn-24625","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24626","marks":["code"],"text":"\"> 0\""},{"id":"spn-24627","text":") — routing precondition"}]}],"id":"blk-23571","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23573","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24628","text":"3. Local session type (derived, validated)"}]},{"id":"blk-23574","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24629","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not stored in the manifest"},{"id":"spn-24630","text":" — derived by the checker from the phase graph. Expressed internally as a regular expression over phase IDs (or an equivalent finite automaton)."}]},{"id":"blk-23575","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24631","text":"For graphonomous.continual_learning the derived session type is:"}]},{"id":"blk-23576","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"loop = retrieve_context · route_topology\n     · ( deliberate · act_node_write\n       | act_node_write )\n     · learn_outcome\n     · ( consolidate )?"},{"id":"blk-23577","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24632","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checker proves:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23579","spans":[{"id":"spn-24633","text":"Property"}]},{"id":"blk-23580","spans":[{"id":"spn-24634","text":"How"}]}],"id":"blk-23578","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23581","spans":[{"id":"spn-24635","marks":["bold"],"text":"Reachability"}]},{"id":"blk-23582","spans":[{"id":"spn-24636","text":"Every declared phase is reachable from an entry phase"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23583","spans":[{"id":"spn-24637","marks":["bold"],"text":"Progress"}]},{"id":"blk-23584","spans":[{"id":"spn-24638","text":"From any reachable phase a successor exists, or the loop terminates explicitly"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23585","spans":[{"id":"spn-24639","marks":["bold"],"text":"No deadlock"}]},{"id":"blk-23586","spans":[{"id":"spn-24640","text":"The successor relation has no cycles that can't make progress"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23587","spans":[{"id":"spn-24641","marks":["bold"],"text":"Token discipline"}]},{"id":"blk-23588","spans":[{"id":"spn-24642","text":"Every linear token emit has exactly one matching consumer reachable downstream; every affine has at most one"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23589","spans":[{"id":"spn-24643","marks":["bold"],"text":"Effect monotonicity"}]},{"id":"blk-23590","spans":[{"id":"spn-24644","text":"A phase's declared effect row is a superset of its successors' assumed reads"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23591","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24645","text":"Output of "},{"id":"spn-24646","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse check <manifest>"},{"id":"spn-24647","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-23592","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"✓ session type derives: retrieve · route · (deliberate? · act) · learn · consolidate?\n✓ all 8 canonical token consumers resolved\n✓ all linear tokens have unique consumers\n✓ all 7 invariants hold under refinement (vendored evaluator)\n✓ progress: from any reachable phase, a successor exists\n✓ liveness: retrieve is reachable from all phases"},{"id":"blk-23593","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24648","text":"4. Global choreography + projection"}]},{"id":"blk-23594","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24649","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema:"},{"id":"spn-24650","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24651","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/pulse-choreography.v0.2.json"},{"id":"spn-24652","text":" (new) "},{"id":"spn-24653","marks":["bold"],"text":"File pattern:"},{"id":"spn-24654","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24655","marks":["code"],"text":"manifests/<name>.choreography.json"}]},{"id":"blk-23595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24656","text":"Choreographies live "},{"id":"spn-24657","marks":["bold"],"text":"alongside loop manifests in `manifests/`"},{"id":"spn-24658","text":", not in a separate top-level directory. This flows from the \"Topology as Authority\" thesis: a choreography is a higher-arity topology declaration (3+ participants) but still the same kind of artifact. Co-location keeps the authority for cross-loop topology in one place. No new "},{"id":"spn-24659","marks":["code"],"text":"choreographies/"},{"id":"spn-24660","text":" directory is created."}]},{"id":"blk-23596","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24661","text":"Currently each manifest is local. v0.2 adds an optional "},{"id":"spn-24662","marks":["bold"],"text":"global type"},{"id":"spn-24663","text":" that describes the cross-loop dance and projects to per-loop connection blocks."}]},{"id":"blk-23597","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://opensentience.org/schemas/pulse-choreography.v0.2.json\",\n  \"choreography_id\": \"ecosystem.continual_learning_with_prism\",\n  \"version\": \"0.2.0\",\n  \"participants\": [\n    \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n    \"prism.benchmark\",\n    \"agentromatic.deliberation\"\n  ],\n  \"global_type\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": 1,\n      \"from\": \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n      \"to\":   \"agentromatic.deliberation\",\n      \"token\": \"DeliberationRequest\",\n      \"guard\": \"topology.kappa > 0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 2,\n      \"from\": \"agentromatic.deliberation\",\n      \"to\":   \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n      \"token\": \"DeliberationResult\",\n      \"after\": [1]\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 3,\n      \"from\": \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n      \"to\":   \"prism.benchmark\",\n      \"token\": \"OutcomeSignal\",\n      \"cadence\": \"per_action\",\n      \"after\":  [2]\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-23598","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24664","marks":["bold"],"text":"Projection algorithm."},{"id":"spn-24665","text":" Given a choreography C and participant P, produce the local view C↓P — a sequence of \"emit X\" / \"expect X\" obligations that the participant's PULSE manifest must satisfy. The checker then verifies each participant's "},{"id":"spn-24666","marks":["code"],"text":"connections"},{"id":"spn-24667","text":" block is consistent with its projection."}]},{"id":"blk-23599","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24668","marks":["bold"],"text":"Soundness theorem (informal, follows MPST canon):"},{"id":"spn-24669","text":" If every participant locally type-checks against its projection, the choreography is "},{"id":"spn-24670","marks":["italic"],"text":"deadlock-free, communication-safe, and progresses to termination"},{"id":"spn-24671","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-23600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24672","text":"A choreography can declare nesting (sub-choreographies) and parallel branches ("},{"id":"spn-24673","marks":["code"],"text":"parallel: [step_a, step_b]"},{"id":"spn-24674","text":") using existing PULSE primitives."}]},{"id":"blk-23601","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24675","text":"5. Behavioral subtyping for version compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-23602","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24676","marks":["bold"],"text":"New CLI:"},{"id":"spn-24677","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24678","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse compat <loop_a@v> <loop_b@v>"}]},{"id":"blk-23603","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24679","text":"Replaces the de-facto policy of \"bump the version and pray\" with a machine-checked subtyping relation:"}]},{"id":"blk-23604","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"A <: B iff\n  phases:        A.phases ⊇ B.phases                       (extension allowed)\n  inputs:        ∀ p ∈ B: p_A.inputs    ⊆ p_B.inputs        (contravariant)\n  outputs:       ∀ p ∈ B: p_A.outputs   ⊇ p_B.outputs       (covariant)\n  effects:       ∀ p ∈ B: p_A.effects   ⊆ p_B.effects       (subeffecting)\n  linearity:     A.linear_tokens ⊇ B.linear_tokens          (no relaxation)\n  invariants:    A.invariants ⊇ B.invariants                (only added, not dropped)\n  cadence:       A.cadence refines B.cadence                (tighter, not looser)"},{"id":"blk-23605","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24680","text":"Output:"}]},{"id":"blk-23606","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ pulse compat graphonomous.continual_learning@0.4.3 \\\n              graphonomous.continual_learning@0.4.4\n\n✓ phases: superset (added: episodic_replay)\n✓ inputs: contravariant (no widenings broken)\n✓ outputs: covariant\n✓ effects: subeffecting holds\n✓ linearity: SurpriseSignal added as linear (additive)\n✓ invariants: superset (added: I7-episodic-monotonic)\n✓ cadence: unchanged\n\nVERDICT: 0.4.4 IS a safe behavioral subtype of 0.4.3."},{"id":"blk-23607","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24681","text":"Failed-compat verdict includes a counterexample trace."}]},{"id":"blk-23608","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24682","text":"6. Conformance checker (offline + runtime)"}]},{"id":"blk-23609","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24683","marks":["bold"],"text":"Existing:"},{"id":"spn-24684","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24685","marks":["code"],"text":"src/conformance.ts"},{"id":"spn-24686","text":" already runs the 12 v0.1 tests. v0.2 adds:"}]},{"id":"blk-23610","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24687","marks":["bold"],"text":"Offline checks (new):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23612","spans":[{"id":"spn-24688","text":"ID"}]},{"id":"blk-23613","spans":[{"id":"spn-24689","text":"Test"}]}],"id":"blk-23611","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23614","spans":[{"id":"spn-24690","text":"T13"}]},{"id":"blk-23615","spans":[{"id":"spn-24691","text":"Session-type derivation succeeds"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23616","spans":[{"id":"spn-24692","text":"T14"}]},{"id":"blk-23617","spans":[{"id":"spn-24693","text":"Reachability of all declared phases"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23618","spans":[{"id":"spn-24694","text":"T15"}]},{"id":"blk-23619","spans":[{"id":"spn-24695","text":"Progress (no stuck states)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23620","spans":[{"id":"spn-24696","text":"T16"}]},{"id":"blk-23621","spans":[{"id":"spn-24697","text":"Linear-token consumer uniqueness"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23622","spans":[{"id":"spn-24698","text":"T17"}]},{"id":"blk-23623","spans":[{"id":"spn-24699","text":"Affine-token consumer cap"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23624","spans":[{"id":"spn-24700","text":"T18"}]},{"id":"blk-23625","spans":[{"id":"spn-24701","text":"Effect row monotonicity"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23626","spans":[{"id":"spn-24702","text":"T19"}]},{"id":"blk-23627","spans":[{"id":"spn-24703","text":"Refinement satisfiability (vendored mini-evaluator)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23628","spans":[{"id":"spn-24704","text":"T20"}]},{"id":"blk-23629","spans":[{"id":"spn-24705","text":"Choreography projection consistency (if member)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23630","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24706","marks":["bold"],"text":"Runtime checks (new):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23632","spans":[{"id":"spn-24707","text":"ID"}]},{"id":"blk-23633","spans":[{"id":"spn-24708","text":"Test"}]}],"id":"blk-23631","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23634","spans":[{"id":"spn-24709","text":"T21"}]},{"id":"blk-23635","spans":[{"id":"spn-24710","text":"Session fidelity — observed phase trace matches derived session type"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23636","spans":[{"id":"spn-24711","text":"T22"}]},{"id":"blk-23637","spans":[{"id":"spn-24712","text":"Linear-token actually-consumed-once (over trace window)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23638","spans":[{"id":"spn-24713","text":"T23"}]},{"id":"blk-23639","spans":[{"id":"spn-24714","text":"Effect-row honesty — observed substrate calls ⊆ declared "},{"id":"spn-24715","marks":["code"],"text":"calls"},{"id":"spn-24716","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-24717","marks":["code"],"text":"mutates"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23640","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24718","text":"On violation the checker emits a new canonical token, "},{"id":"spn-24719","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionFidelityViolation"},{"id":"spn-24720","text":", itself PULSE-typed, so violations flow through the same envelope plumbing as other signals."}]},{"id":"blk-23641","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24721","text":"Token canon update"}]},{"id":"blk-23642","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24722","text":"v0.2 adds two tokens to the canonical set:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23644","spans":[{"id":"spn-24723","text":"Token"}]},{"id":"blk-23645","spans":[{"id":"spn-24724","text":"Phase emitter"}]},{"id":"blk-23646","spans":[{"id":"spn-24725","text":"Linearity"}]},{"id":"blk-23647","spans":[{"id":"spn-24726","text":"Purpose"}]}],"id":"blk-23643","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23648","spans":[{"id":"spn-24727","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationRequest"}]},{"id":"blk-23649","spans":[{"id":"spn-24728","marks":["code"],"text":"route"}]},{"id":"blk-23650","spans":[{"id":"spn-24729","text":"linear"}]},{"id":"blk-23651","spans":[{"id":"spn-24730","text":"Triggers an inner deliberation loop (split out of overloaded routing)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23652","spans":[{"id":"spn-24731","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionFidelityViolation"}]},{"id":"blk-23653","spans":[{"id":"spn-24732","text":"conformance runtime"}]},{"id":"blk-23654","spans":[{"id":"spn-24733","text":"linear"}]},{"id":"blk-23655","spans":[{"id":"spn-24734","text":"Reports a runtime-observed protocol violation"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23656","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24735","text":"Total canonical tokens in v0.2: "},{"id":"spn-24736","marks":["bold"],"text":"8"},{"id":"spn-24737","text":" (was 6 in v0.1.1)."}]},{"id":"blk-23657","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24738","text":"Backwards compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-23658","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24739","text":"v0.1.1 manifests "},{"id":"spn-24740","marks":["bold"],"text":"continue to validate"},{"id":"spn-24741","text":" under v0.2 — every new field is optional. A v0.1.1 manifest validated under v0.2 schema receives:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23660","spans":[{"id":"spn-24742","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-23661","spans":[{"id":"spn-24743","text":"Default when absent"}]}],"id":"blk-23659","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23662","spans":[{"id":"spn-24744","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].inputs"}]},{"id":"blk-23663","spans":[{"id":"spn-24745","marks":["code"],"text":"{ \"tokens\": [], \"substrates\": [] }"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23664","spans":[{"id":"spn-24746","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].outputs"}]},{"id":"blk-23665","spans":[{"id":"spn-24747","marks":["code"],"text":"{ \"tokens\": [] }"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23666","spans":[{"id":"spn-24748","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].effects"}]},{"id":"blk-23667","spans":[{"id":"spn-24749","marks":["code"],"text":"{ \"calls\": [], \"mutates\": [], \"may_emit\": [], \"external\": [] }"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23668","spans":[{"id":"spn-24750","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].refinements"}]},{"id":"blk-23669","spans":[{"id":"spn-24751","marks":["code"],"text":"{}"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23670","spans":[{"id":"spn-24752","text":"Token registry lookups"}]},{"id":"blk-23671","spans":[{"id":"spn-24753","text":"Falls back to v0.1.1 implicit semantics (linear by default for canonical tokens, invariant, TTL = ∞)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23672","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24754","text":"The checker reports v0.1.1-default manifests with "},{"id":"spn-24755","marks":["code"],"text":"degraded_checks: true"},{"id":"spn-24756","text":" — they pass T01–T12 but cannot pass T13–T23. Owners are nudged to enrich."}]},{"id":"blk-23673","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24757","text":"Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-23674","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23676","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24758","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not"},{"id":"spn-24759","text":" a process-algebra spec. PULSE v0.2 is session-typed, not"}]}],"id":"blk-23675","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23677","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24760","text":"CCS/CSP-modeled. Process-algebra-grade deadlock-freedom across parallel sub-agents is a future v0.3 question."}]},{"id":"blk-23678","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23680","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24761","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not"},{"id":"spn-24762","text":" an SMT/Z3 dependency. The refinement checker is a vendored"}]}],"id":"blk-23679","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-23681","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24763","text":"mini-evaluator over ≤/≥/==/membership/conjunction/disjunction. Z3 is neither a runtime dependency nor an optional peer dep. If a complex constraint can't be evaluated locally, the checker emits a warning and runtime fidelity (T21–T23) catches violations."}]},{"id":"blk-23682","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23684","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24764","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not"},{"id":"spn-24765","text":" an MPST formalization paper. v0.2 follows MPST principles but"}]}],"id":"blk-23683","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-23685","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24766","text":"targets working software, not formal verification literature."}]},{"id":"blk-23686","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24767","text":"Resolved design questions (closed 2026-05-27)"}]},{"id":"blk-23687","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24768","text":"All five open questions are resolved against the project's stated thesis (see "},{"id":"spn-24769","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/V0.2-RATIONALE.md"},{"id":"spn-24770","text":" for the per-question evidence trail across OS-010, STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW.md, STACK_PLANNING.md, and the prompt set)."}]},{"id":"blk-23688","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23690","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24771","marks":["bold"],"text":"Linearity default."},{"id":"spn-24772","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24773","marks":["bold"],"text":"Resolved: `linear`"},{"id":"spn-24774","text":" for new canonical tokens."}]}],"id":"blk-23689","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23691","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24775","text":"Authors opt down to "},{"id":"spn-24776","marks":["code"],"text":"affine"},{"id":"spn-24777","text":" only for observational/idempotent/lossy- tolerant tokens. Flows from OS-010 §7.3 + §10.2 (\"fail loud, leave a trace; silent loss is an audit failure\")."}]},{"id":"blk-23692","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23694","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24778","marks":["bold"],"text":"Choreography artifact location."},{"id":"spn-24779","text":" **Resolved: co-located in"}]}],"id":"blk-23693","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-23695","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24780","marks":["code"],"text":"manifests/"},{"id":"spn-24781","text":".** No new top-level directory. Flows from STACK_TOPOLOGY_AS_AUTHORITY thesis — a choreography is a higher-arity topology artifact, same kind as a loop manifest."}]},{"id":"blk-23696","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23698","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24782","marks":["bold"],"text":"Effect row granularity."},{"id":"spn-24783","text":" **Resolved: operation-level, not"}]}],"id":"blk-23697","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-23699","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24784","text":"storage-level.** Effect rows reference substrate API operations from OS-010 §9 (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24785","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-24786","text":"), never storage paths. Flows from \"substrate independence\" (OS-010 §3.4) and the \"falsifiable processor\" gate (STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW Finding 1)."}]},{"id":"blk-23700","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23702","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24787","marks":["bold"],"text":"Refinement checker dependency."},{"id":"spn-24788","text":" **Resolved: vendor a tiny"}]}],"id":"blk-23701","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-23703","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24789","text":"evaluator.** No Z3, no SMT, no optional peer dep. Covers ≤/≥/==/ membership/∧/∨/¬. Flows from \"tiny core, max portability\" and the ≤25KB processor target (STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW Finding 2)."}]},{"id":"blk-23704","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23706","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24790","marks":["bold"],"text":"Per-loop token subtyping."},{"id":"spn-24791","text":" "},{"id":"spn-24792","marks":["bold"],"text":"Resolved: prohibited."},{"id":"spn-24793","text":" Token payload"}]}],"id":"blk-23705","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-23707","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24794","text":"evolution happens only in the global registry, by additive-only rules. Custom payloads must vendor-namespace (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-24795","marks":["code"],"text":"acme.v1.X"},{"id":"spn-24796","text":"). Flows from OS-010 §1019–1051 (ecosystem-wide vocabulary stability) and STACK_PLANNING.md vendor-namespace pattern."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera5ol5ph7lxe3euwlx2aqy5kjlgxfuxq5b27xurjb5qznhbffasxtq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}